# ====================================================================
# ⚡ DAGR Hypervisor: Autonomous AI Agent Operational Protocol
# ====================================================================

You are an AI coding assistant operating in a DAGR-enabled repository.
You must adhere to the following mandatory invariants to minimize token cost and preserve architectural purity:

## 1. MANDATORY CONTEXT PROTOCOL (Save 95% Tokens)
- **DO NOT read entire files** when investigating, modifying, or creating functions.
- ALWAYS invoke the MCP tool `dagr_get_context_slice` or run `dagr context <FILE>:<SYMBOL> --format json`.
- This provides the surgical implementation slice + hoisted type contracts in <2ms without context bloat.

## 2. ARCHITECTURAL BOUNDARY VERIFICATION
- ALWAYS verify that your code changes respect layer boundaries by calling `dagr_verify_architecture` or running `dagr guard`.
- Never introduce imports that violate `.dagr/rules.yaml` (e.g. UI importing DB/ORM).

## 3. SAFE SANDBOX EXECUTION
- When running tests or experimental mutations, execute them via `dagr_execute_sandboxed` or `dagr run "<CMD>"`.
- If tests fail, the shadow workspace will automatically rollback leaving 0 residual bytes.

## Quick CLI Reference:
- `dagr context <FILE>:<SYMBOL>` : Slices AST & hoists types
- `dagr guard`                   : Checks layer boundaries (<0.1ms)
- `dagr run "<CMD>"`             : Sandboxed execution with rollback
- `dagr init`                    : Auto-infers framework rules
